<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18364" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">flexĭlis</span></b> , e, adj.
		flexus, from flecto. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Pliant</i>, <i>pliable</i>, <i>flexile</i> (<b>poet.</b> and in
			postAug. prose): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cornu,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					5, 383</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ulmus et fraxinus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					16, 40, 79, § 219</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">betulla,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					16, 18, 30, § 75</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cervix ad circumspectum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					11, 37, 67, § 177</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vitrum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					36, 26, 66, § 195</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lectuli,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 22, 4</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Bent</i>, <i>curved</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">spicae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 6 <i>init.</i></span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">Ov. Am. 1, 14, 26</span></i>, read nexilis,
			Merk.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
